  "title": "CHAPTER 3: POLITY AND ADMINISTRATION OF GOA",
  "order": 3,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "5v0cwsa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.1 Constitutional Status of Goa"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Goa's political identity was preserved through the landmark historic Opinion Poll of 1967, rejecting merger with Maharashtra.",
        "The constitutional status of Goa evolved from a Union Territory to becoming the 25th state of India via the 56th Constitutional Amendment Act in 1987.",
        "Local Self-Government in Goa is divided into Panchayati Raj institutions for rural governance and Urban Local Bodies for towns and cities.",
        "The Goa Public Service Commission (GPSC) functions as the apex constitutional body responsible for recruiting civil servants under Article 315.",
        "Goa Police Organisation handles law enforcement, public safety, and administrative order across the state's districts."
      ],
      "id": "2rts78w"
    },
