    {
      "id": "bduoqcc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.2 Opinion Poll of 1967"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lvu7qtj",
      "content": "The Opinion Poll of January 16, 1967 was a historic democratic exercise to decide whether Goa should merge with Maharashtra (as demanded by Maharashtrawadi Gomantak Party) or remain a Union Territory."
    },
    {
      "id": "96l851n",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Date: January 16, 1967",
        "Question: Should Goa merge with Maharashtra or remain a separate Union Territory?",
        "Result: 54.18% voted to remain separate; 45.82% voted for merger",
        "This was only the second time a referendum/opinion poll was held in independent India (first was for merger of Sikkim)",
        "The result affirmed Goan identity and eventually paved the way for statehood"
      ]
    },
    {
